body:
`packages/core/src/adapters/index.d.ts` (and `packages/core/src/index.d.ts`) still export `ObjectStackAdapter` / `createObjectStackAdapter`, but this file no longer exports them. That creates a runtime/types mismatch (TypeScript allows imports that will be `undefined` at runtime). Either remove/regen the `.d.ts` exports to match the new behavior, or keep a real export here (e.g., re-export from `@object-ui/data-objectstack` or provide a deprecated shim that throws a clear error).
```suggestion
// Adapters have been moved to separate packages (e.g. @object-ui/data-objectstack)
// These exports are kept as deprecated shims to avoid a runtime/types mismatch
// with existing .d.ts declarations. They throw to guide users to the new package.

/**
 * @deprecated
 * Adapters have moved to @object-ui/data-objectstack.
 *
 * Instead of:
 *   import { ObjectStackAdapter } from '@object-ui/core/adapters';
 *
 * Use:
 *   import { ObjectStackAdapter } from '@object-ui/data-objectstack';
 */
export class ObjectStackAdapter {
  constructor() {
    throw new Error(
      '[ObjectUI] ObjectStackAdapter has moved to @object-ui/data-objectstack. ' +
        'Please install that package and import ObjectStackAdapter from there.'
    );
  }
}

/**
 * @deprecated
 * Adapters have moved to @object-ui/data-objectstack.
 *
 * Instead of:
 *   import { createObjectStackAdapter } from '@object-ui/core/adapters';
 *
 * Use:
 *   import { createObjectStackAdapter } from '@object-ui/data-objectstack';
 */
export function createObjectStackAdapter() {
  throw new Error(
    '[ObjectUI] createObjectStackAdapter has moved to @object-ui/data-objectstack. ' +
      'Please install that package and import createObjectStackAdapter from there.'
  );
}
```
